  "examples": [
    {
      "coptic": "ⲛⲁϣ ⲛϩⲉ ⲉϥⲛⲁⲉⲩⲫⲣⲁⲛⲉ · ⲉϥϩⲩⲡⲟⲕⲓⲥⲑⲉ ⲉⲧⲣⲉⲟⲩⲧⲃⲛⲏ ⲉⲓ ⲉϫⲱϥ ⲛϥⲣⲁϩⲧϥ ⲛϥⲙⲟⲩ · ⲁⲩⲱ ⲣⲱϥ ⲡⲏϣ ⲛϫⲓϩ ϩⲓ**ⲉⲓⲧⲛ** · ϩⲓⲧⲙⲡⲥⲩⲣⲁ ϩⲓⲡⲉⲥⲏⲧ ·",
      "english": "In what way then doth he rejoice? He is liable to be attacked by some beast, which will trample him to death, and will split open his head, and the foam of his mouth and his intestines will be scattered about on the herbage (?) and on the ground.",
      "source": "On the Soul and Body",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:psathanasius.soul_body.budge:1-91",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲛⲉϫ ⲇⲉ ⲛⲁϣⲏ ⲛ**ⲉⲓⲧⲛ** ⲉⲡϫⲓⲥⲉ ⲉⲁⲩⲛⲟϭ ⲛϣⲟⲉⲓϣ ⲧⲱⲟⲩⲛ ⲉϫⲱⲓ ·",
      "english": "now they ejected a lot of dung on my back, and threw up very much dust about me,",
      "source": "Life of Pisentius part 3",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.pisentius.budge:58-84",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲉϣⲱⲡⲉ ⲇⲉ ⲧⲉⲕⲁⲙⲉⲗⲓⲁ ⲧⲉⲧⲥⲱⲕ ⲙⲙⲟⲕ ⲉⲓⲉⲣⲓⲙⲉ ⲛⲅⲛⲉϩⲡⲉ · ϫⲉⲛⲉⲧⲟⲩϩⲗⲟⲟⲗⲉ ⲙⲙⲟⲟⲩ ϩⲓϫⲛⲛⲕⲟⲕⲕⲟⲥ · ⲁⲩϭⲟⲟⲗⲟⲩ ⲙⲡⲉⲓ**ⲉⲓⲧⲛ** ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ϫⲉⲁⲩⲁⲙⲉⲗⲉⲓ ⲉⲡⲛⲟⲙⲟⲥ ⲙⲡⲛⲟⲩⲧⲉ · ⲉⲁⲩⲟⲩⲁϩⲟⲩ ⲛⲥⲁⲡⲟⲩⲱϣ ⲙⲡⲉⲩϩⲏⲧ ·",
      "english": "Now if it be thy carelessness which draweth thee to weeping, thou shalt mourn ; for those who wear scarlet shall clothe themselves with dung, because they have been careless concerning the Law of God, and have followed after the desires of their hearts.",
